c(33, "§4.2 table (verbatim); §4.2; §4.3; §4.4; §4.5", "data-caveat", "Themes by star band (verbatim): " + table("## 4.2 Themes by star band", 0) + " — PR_DESIGN appears in every band (10.6% of 1★ still praise the design: 'beauty does not protect the rating; it is what makes the failure worth writing about'); U:reliability is the strongest gradient (38.71% of 1★ vs 4.41% of 5★) — the rating-determining theme; MON_PAID_EXPLICIT roughly flat (16.13% of 1★, 9.74% of 5★) — 'paying does not make people kind'; paywall_complaint 31.34% of 1★ but 4.1% of 5★. 5★: 84 (8.62%) also report a defect and 40 contain no praise at all; 4★ is the 'almost' band — request_any 47.48%, praise + one named missing thing (Watch, widget, iPad, overview), RATING_LEVERAGE 16 ('I'll be sure to change my rating to 5 stars when the updates come out!'); 3★ the most diagnostic — bug_any 57.71%, DEV_STALE 8% ('Great, when working').", "n/a", "mixed", "reliability 38.71% of 1★ vs 4.41% of 5★; 4★ request 47.48%; RATING_LEVERAGE 16", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["3018036105", "1819603242", "2186159961", "5642646849", "7936221496"], "", "")

c(34, "§4.6 table (verbatim); §4.6", "timeline", "One- and two-star (verbatim): " + table("## 4.6 One- and two-star", 0) + " — two populations separated by time: in 2016 a 1★ is a paywall objection from someone who never got to use the app ('Free version is worthless. You can only have 1 habit'); from 2018 a 1★ is a long-term user whose app broke ('It has become increasingly slow with every update. Now it's unusable… I've contacted support multiple times over the past 6 months', 2022) — 'the second kind is far more costly: those reviewers had already paid'.", "n/a", "1★-burst", "1★ 217; 2★ 100", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["1346034110", "8580429365", "1606690337", "3924163363"], "", "")

c(35, "§4.7 table (verbatim); §4.7", "data-caveat", "Rating-vs-text contradictions: CONTRA_RATING 46 (2.58%) (verbatim): " + table("## 4.7 Rating-versus-text", 0) + " — 40 are 5★ whose text is only a complaint ('Blank Screen after IOS update' — entire text; 'the widget has a bug on iOS 10; purple blocks keep appearing'; 'it's OK, but why do I have to pay to go past three?') vs 4 low-star positives; 'the public 4.5–4.8★ average is inflated relative to written sentiment not only by silent star-tappers but by a measurable population of users who write a complaint and tap five stars anyway'.", "n/a", "mixed", "CONTRA 46 / 2.58%: 40 5★-complaints, 4 low-star-positive", "none", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["9309917073", "1548898250", "1611850727", "1476921895", "1460920237"], "", "")

c(36, "§5.1; §5.2 table (verbatim); §5.2; §5.6", "data-caveat", "Paid population: 188 (10.53%) state they paid, mean 3.69★ vs 3.97; not a conversion rate (mentioning payment is itself selective); MON_WILLBUY 43 (2.41%). Segment rates (verbatim): " + table("## 5.2 Segment rates", 0) + " — paid reviewers report defects at a higher rate (bug_any 34.57% vs 26.27%: they use it more, longer, with more habits — the condition under which the app degrades); they carry the data-loss complaint disproportionately (backup is paid; 12 of 55 data-loss reviewers paid — 'selling backup and then losing data is the corpus's sharpest breach of trust'); they defend the pricing (PR_ONETIME, PR_WORTH, MON_DEFEND far above global). Cannot claim conversion, ARPU, churn, that the tier change drove purchases, or anything about the ~2022 subscription (59 + 13 reviews).", "n/a", "mixed", "PAID 188 / 10.53% / 3.69★; paid bug_any 34.57%; WILLBUY 43", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["2955539119", "1454413050"], "", "")

c(37, "§5.3 table (verbatim); §5.3", "insight", "What triggers a purchase — MON_TRIGGER 18 (verbatim): " + table("## 5.3 What triggers a purchase", 0) + " — more habits ('I wanted more habits, so I use the paid version', jp), custom cover photos ('just because to put my own photo covers'), the cards ('little motivation boards was what made me pay'), the developer listening ('because they actually listened… I just paid full price'), the Watch app, one specific premium card ('to calculate my stress level'), supporting the developer (MON_SUPPORT_DEV 8); 'people buy to remove the habit cap, and they buy for the visual/customisation layer. Nobody reports buying for backup, for the passcode lock, or for statistics — even though backup and the lock are premium'.", "cap + covers + cards convert; backup/lock/stats do not", "purchase-driver", "MON_TRIGGER 18; SUPPORT_DEV 8", "build-paid", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["1454413050", "1483615798", "1347650463", "1351843491", "1951004228", "3555120788", "1364442019"], "", "the paid features that convert are the ones users can see; the ones they cannot see (backup, lock) convert no one")

c(38, "§5.4 table (verbatim); §5.4; §8.2", "must-never-break", "What goes wrong after purchase — U:purchase_friction 51 (2.86%, 2.61★) (verbatim): " + table("## 5.4 What goes wrong", 0) + " — MON_RESTORE 18 (2016-03-28 → 2021-02-12), a nine-year unresolved defect attacking paying customers: 'I bought it last year — why does it charge again after reinstalling?'; 'I delete the app, now I install it again (on the same phone) and I have to buy the features again'; '¿Es una estafa?' (1★); 'I paid for the Premium twice' (2★); one found Settings → Restore Purchases himself — 'the function exists and is undiscoverable'; the March 2018 purchase outage: 5 reviews, mostly Chinese, report the IAP 'no longer available' ('I am trying to give you $4.99… It keeps failing. I wrote for help and no response', 1★); MON_REGRESS 3 — features taken back after purchase ('you have to pay to use your own pictures and completely took everything i had on my profile off to do so', 2023; a one-time buyer 'now unable to manage habits at all', 2026); MON_REFUND 7, two report Apple refusing.", "restore undiscoverable; IAP outage; paid features withdrawn", "1★-burst", "purchase_friction 51 / 2.61★; RESTORE 18; IAP_FAIL 11; REGRET 12; REFUND 7; OVERCHARGE 2; REGRESS 3", "must-never-break", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["1698805807", "5727531937", "6868594425", "13517933118", "2274068869", "2284049297", "2568596703", "9814749006", "14015405307"], "", "")

c(39, "§5.5 table (verbatim); §5.5", "monetization", "Upgrade barriers — MON_WILLBUY 43 is the most actionable code, people saying exactly what would make them pay (verbatim): " + table("## 5.5 Upgrade barriers", 0) + " — fix the Watch, ship a widget ('they urgently need a widget and I swear I'd pay premium'), an iPad version, every-N-days frequency ('I would rate it 5 stars and purchase the full version'), weekday-only reminders ('I'll pay immediately'), a comprehensible UI, a fixed gallery, 'just update the app'; and the trial objection — MON_TRIAL_REQ 33 (1.85%): 'Expand the free app to allow a proper trial and then ask for money' (2016); 'one is not enough for a trial' (2024) — 'eight years apart, the same sentence'.", "1-habit free tier as the only trial", "blocked-conversion", "WILLBUY 43 / 2.41%; TRIAL_REQ 33 / 1.85%", "research", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["1637702429", "10949219510", "9820894783", "1494360640", "2492317967", "7249989187", "5535282962", "4957079710", "1346019622", "1346522458"], "", "")

